0..79 Comment "// A record type\'s faces: each a set of the record\'s labels, named in a `where`"
80..158 Comment "// block after the type. A static bracket after the type fixes some fields, by"
159..236 Comment "// label, by face, or by a system of faces. In a system, the checker converts"
237..308 Comment "// each later face\'s value on a meet with the first face\'s value there."
309..311 Comment "//"
312..389 Comment "// A record type\'s labels are its boundary, and a face over them names a part"
390..466 Comment "// of the record. The checker checks each fixed value at its field\'s type. A"
467..543 Comment "// value of the patched type is the record of its free fields, and a literal"
544..624 Comment "// can state a fixed field at its fixed value. A value of the record type stands"
625..703 Comment "// at the patched type when each fixed field converts with its fixed value. An"
704..781 Comment "// element of the patched type stands at the record type as its record, and a"
782..823 Comment "// selection reads a fixed field\'s value."
824..826 Comment "//"
827..904 Comment "// The block names each face as a theory\'s `face` member does. The block ends"
905..984 Comment "// the type member at its `}`, as a `data` block ends its declaration. A record"
985..1053 Comment "// type with no block keeps its labels as its boundary all the same."
1054..1122 Comment "// `Config[.port = 443, .tls = true]` fixes two fields by label, and"
1123..1199 Comment "// `Config[secure ↦ *{.port = 443, .tls = true}]` fixes the face `secure`."
1200..1231 Comment "// `|->` spells `↦` in ASCII."
1232..1234 Comment "//"
1235..1313 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/record-faces.gandr` — a face past the labels, a"
1314..1389 Comment "//   face named twice, a bracket naming a field or a face the type lacks, a"
1390..1461 Comment "//   literal stating a fixed field at another value, and two faces that"
1462..1498 Comment "//   disagree on their meet, refused"
1499..1578 Comment "// - see: `model/desc/shaped-signature.gandr` — a theory\'s `boundary` and its"
1579..1589 Comment "//   faces"
